MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_001: I will kill all who stand in my way... Every last one...\nwill die by my hand!
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_029: 
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_002: Ah! N-no! This can't... I can't...
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_003: Huh?!
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_030: 
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_004: Promised One... I am sorry. My bow. I dropped it\nin battle. There is no excuse.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_005: <NCA>"What happened?"
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_006: I felt...afraid. Like I wasn't me.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_007: It felt like...I was wielding Ugo's Bow again. Balor's\nvoice was in my head, snuffing me out.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_008: The desire to kill had a will of its own. To almost be\nreduced to that...
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_009: <NCA>"Are you alright?"
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_010: <NCB>"Try not to push yourself so hard."
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_011: <ACA>Yes. I am well. Because you are here.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_012: <ACB>Thank you, but...I am not pushing myself. I can fight.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_013: Yet...every time I fight and defeat our enemies it\ntakes a toll. And I become afraid.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_014: Afraid that I am losing myself... Becoming more\nevil, like Balor.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_015: Even so, I will keep fighting by your side.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_016: I want to help save the world and ease suffering.\nI refuse to abandon people in need.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_017: But given what just happened, I'm not sure you can\ncount on me in the battles ahead.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_018: <NCA>"I'm glad you're by my side."
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_019: Ah! How kind. I'm grateful to hear you say so.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_020: You have saved me so many times. I only hope I can\nreturn the favor.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_021: It is only by the grace of those around me that I've\nrecovered from Balor's influence.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_022: After the Heroic Games, when I lost that part of\nBalor I had, I was but a shell of a person.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_023: You all befriended me, a stranger. I cannot thank\nyou enough.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_024: Which is why I refuse to abandon a single soul. I do\nnot care for war, but I must fight.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_025: Some old friends from my village came a long way\nto fight too. They agree. We must all help each other.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_026: <NCA>"You have good friends."
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_027: Yes! And I have you, Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_A_028: I hope to save someone someday, like you and the\nothers saved me. Whatever it takes, I'll do it.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_001: Please, please... Be alive, wherever you are...\nBe safe and sound.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_002: <NCA>"I have returned."
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_003: Promised One! I've been waiting here, hoping as\nhard as I could... This is truly a blessing!
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_004: <NCA>"I see some things packed up here..."
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_005: Many of my friends from back home died in the\nfight. I gathered their possessions. It's a lot, isn't it?
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_006: Some died fighting the dead, but the rest here...\nThey couldn't cope with seeing our friends die...
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_007: The war went on for too long...
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_008: My friends who did survive can't bring themselves to\ngo home. They're too wounded—inside and outside.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_009: May there never again be a battle that leaves so\nmany dead and so many wounded.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_010: <NCA>"We must all work together to prevent it."
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_011: Yes. Those of us who lived must find a way. We\nowe it to all those who died.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_012: We must join as one—not alone, not isolated—but\ntogether. Then nothing is impossible.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_013: What will you do now?
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_014: <NCA>"There are still people out there who need help."
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_015: Then this is goodbye. And I have my own duty to\nanswer to.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_016: My remaining family and friends are back home.\nI must return all of this to those grieving.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_017: Then I'll help any survivors who are too wounded,\ndeep inside, to return to their previous lives.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_018: Just like I was helped... Easier said than done.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_019: But even in my small way, I would like to help them\nfind their way back...to themselves.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_020: <NCA>"I believe in you."
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_021: <NCB>"You're well prepared for this."
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_022: <ACA>Really? I believe in me too.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_023: <ACB>Yeah. I'll be fine. I have seen the worst, and I know\nhow to make it through.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_024: If it's not too much to ask, could I clasp your hands\nbefore I part from you?
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_025: Please... I hope to be filled with your courage.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_026: <RSDS>Your guiding hand really did save us all, didn't it?
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_027: I won't be able to do nearly as much. But I swear\nto you...I'll do all I can.
MID_SE_Ism_Ini_S_028: And whenever you get back, I'll be here—we'll all be\nhere—to greet you with a smile.